 "area": "retina",
 "description": "MOOD R1 (block 236000) -- the fast appraisal + choice CORE the momentum layer (seeds/mood_r1.json) sits above. A MoodTask node (hung off an EmotionHub by has_mood_task) carries a fast delta-rule value estimate v (a lagging EMA of reward) and a one-offer-per-trial accept/decline choice. Every DECISION is a graph RULE; the world adapter (domains/mood_r1_world.py) only delivers a scalar reward r_t, bumps input_epoch, ticks (run_rules), and reads decision/cum_reward. run_rules is a FIXPOINT loop (a SetAttr stops contributing only when it no longer changes the value), so every accumulating rule SELF-CLOSES on its OWN per-rule epoch marker (input_epoch > e_x guard + set e_x = input_epoch) -- the same idempotent idiom mod_competence/sd_blend use -- firing EXACTLY once per trial regardless of pass semantics. `bias` is a MoodTask attr defaulting to 0; absent the momentum layer mt_learn is a plain delta rule and the whole path is byte-identical to a no-mood world. Loaded for BOTH the WITH-mood and WITHOUT-mood arms. NO Rust, NO new Term (Plus/Minus/Times/Div/IfThenElse/Gt/Attr exist).",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "mood_r1_task",
  "description": "Fast delta-rule value estimate + accept/decline choice as graph rules; the appraisal core mood momentum biases. Reward is a cross-frame observation stream (float); the value EMA is a cross-frame map."
 },
